{"generated_at": "2026-10-16T11:47:07.778772+00:00", "slug": "issue-vouchers-live", "title": "Texas school vouchers, 11 days of posts", "stats": {"posts_processed": 15, "claims": 29, "clusters": 29, "checkable": 22, "verified": 1, "unsupported_spreading": 0, "news_checked": 6, "crossed_over": 3}, "clusters": [{"event": null, "event_type": null, "news": {"articles": 100, "sources": 59, "sources_48h": 31, "articles_48h": 38, "first_news_at": "2026-10-09T08:45:00+00:00", "news_before_x": true, "top_domains": ["politico.com", "nytimes.com", "reuters.com", "nbcnews.com", "cnn.com", "thehill.com"], "covered": true, "checked_at": "2026-10-16T05:52+00:00"}, "id": 20, "text": "Republicans' national school voucher program is a bad idea.", "type": "opinion", "checkable": false, "stance": "against", "entities": ["Republicans"], "verdict": null, "verdict_basis": null, "verdict_sources": [], "posts": 1, "views": 111083, "accounts": 1, "copies": 0, "pushback_posts": 0, "lanes": [{"key": "rural_district_financial_pain", "label": "Vouchers drain rural and public schools", "color": "#d95926", "posts": 1}], "first_seen": "2026-10-14T18:30:39+00:00", "first_handle": "SenMarkKelly", "first_handles": ["SenMarkKelly"], "first_url": "https://x.com/SenMarkKelly/status/2110438149860311399", "first_views": 111083, "last_seen": "2026-10-14T18:30:39+00:00", "views_24h": 0, "series": [["2026-10-14T18:30:39+00:00", 111083]], "top_post": "https://x.com/SenMarkKelly/status/2110438149860311399"}, {"event": null, "event_type": null, "news": {"articles": 44, "sources": 41, "sources_48h": 8, "articles_48h": 9, "first_news_at": "2026-10-09T07:00:00+00:00", "news_before_x": true, "top_domains": ["reuters.com", "dscc.org", "ajc.com", "home.mirs.news", "nationalreview.com", "rawstory.com"], "covered": true, "checked_at": "2026-10-16T05:52+00:00"}, "id": 21, "text": "The Republican national school voucher program drains resources from public schools and benefits the wealthy.", "type": "fact", "checkable": true, "stance": "against", "entities": ["Republicans"], "verdict": "misleading", "verdict_basis": "The claim is a sweeping two-part judgment. The records support parts of it, but not as worded.\n\n- \"National\" program: The federal program is a tax-credit scholarship in the 2025 reconciliation law. It starts in January 2027. Donors get a credit of up to $1,700, and \nscholarship eligibility is limited to students in households at or below 300% of area median income\n. The statute also lets \nthe scholarships fund public school expenses\n. Texas's own ESA/TEFA program is a separate state program, created by SB 2, and it does not come from the federal law.\n- \"Benefits the wealthy\": The Texas data mostly cut against this. The Comptroller's demographic report shows \nabout 80% of funded students come from households below 200% of the federal poverty level\n. Critics have a different point: \n57% of an early set of accepted students were already in private school or homeschool\n, and later data put the share of grade 1–12 awardees at about 70%. Those figures show the money often goes to families who had already left public schools, not that it goes to wealthy families. The Center for American Progress argues the federal credit \nlets wealthier communities generate more donations than low-income ", "verdict_sources": ["https://www.ksat.com/news/local/2026/05/14/more-than-half-of-tefa-recipients-already-enrolled-in-private-or-homeschool-data-shows/", "https://cbsaustin.com/news/local/texas-comptroller-touts-record-school-voucher-rollout-but-critics-cite-missing-details", "https://communityimpact.com/central-austin/texas-legislature/as-lawmakers-consider-expanding-tefa-funding-some-public-schools-say-they-re-losing-money/", "https://www.congress.gov/crs-product/R48724", "https://www.americanprogress.org/article/treasury-regulations-for-the-federal-scholarship-tax-credit-fail-to-protect-students/", "https://ballotpedia.org/State_participation_in_the_federal_K-12_education_tax_credit_program"], "posts": 1, "views": 111083, "accounts": 1, "copies": 0, "pushback_posts": 0, "lanes": [{"key": "rural_district_financial_pain", "label": "Vouchers drain rural and public schools", "color": "#d95926", "posts": 1}], "first_seen": "2026-10-14T18:30:39+00:00", "first_handle": "SenMarkKelly", "first_handles": ["SenMarkKelly"], "first_url": "https://x.com/SenMarkKelly/status/2110438149860311399", "first_views": 111083, "last_seen": "2026-10-14T18:30:39+00:00", "views_24h": 0, "series": [["2026-10-14T18:30:39+00:00", 111083]], "top_post": "https://x.com/SenMarkKelly/status/2110438149860311399"}, {"event": null, "event_type": null, "news": {"articles": 53, "sources": 46, "sources_48h": 11, "articles_48h": 11, "first_news_at": "2026-10-09T12:08:00+00:00", "news_before_x": true, "top_domains": ["vietnam.vn", "myjoyonline.com", "fijivillage.com", "freemalaysiatoday.com", "sandiegouniontribune.com", "tvmnews.mt"], "covered": true, "checked_at": "2026-10-16T05:52+00:00"}, "id": 22, "text": "Every kid deserves a good public education regardless of zip code or parents' income.", "type": "opinion", "checkable": false, "stance": "for", "entities": [], "verdict": null, "verdict_basis": null, "verdict_sources": [], "posts": 1, "views": 111083, "accounts": 1, "copies": 0, "pushback_posts": 0, "lanes": [{"key": "rural_district_financial_pain", "label": "Vouchers drain rural and public schools", "color": "#d95926", "posts": 1}], "first_seen": "2026-10-14T18:30:39+00:00", "first_handle": "SenMarkKelly", "first_handles": ["SenMarkKelly"], "first_url": "https://x.com/SenMarkKelly/status/2110438149860311399", "first_views": 111083, "last_seen": "2026-10-14T18:30:39+00:00", "views_24h": 0, "series": [["2026-10-14T18:30:39+00:00", 111083]], "top_post": "https://x.com/SenMarkKelly/status/2110438149860311399"}, {"event": null, "event_type": null, "news": {"articles": 3, "sources": 3, "sources_48h": 0, "articles_48h": 0, "first_news_at": "2026-10-12T09:00:00+00:00", "news_